    nrt: cache: discardreserved: fix return value
    
    The caches are authoritative regarding the freshness of
    the data they return. This is the intended meaning of the
    boolean return value in the GetCachedNRTCopy signature, kinda
    like "isValid" or "isFresh". So, when there's no data in
    the cache, the information *IS* fresh and should be reported as such.
    
    The cached data is expected to be out of data ("stale", "not fresh",
    "invalid") only when foreign pods (pods running on a node managed
    by the scheduler, but not scheduled by this scheduler) are detected,
    and even so, some cache implementations may tolerate this condition
    and still report valid data.
    
