    * nrt: filter: check node resources out the NUMA loop
    
    In the filtering logic, we check about node-level resource
    availability. We used to do this while iterating over
    the NUMA nodes, but this check is related to node, so
    it is invariant wrt the specific NUMA node.
    
    Let's move this check outside the NUMA loop to save some CPU cycles
    avoiding useless work, and to make the flow clearer.
    
    Signed-off-by: Francesco Romani <fromani@redhat.com>
    
    * nrt: filter: inline resourceFoundOnNode
    
    In the NUMA zone filtering loop, calling
    resourceFoundOnNode repeatedly creates the node-level
    corev1.ResourceList from the nodeInfo.Allocatable.
    
    But nodeinfo.Allocatable is actually a loop invariant,
    so let's inline the function in the (one and only)
    calling site, which allow us to move the corev1.ResourceList
    creation outside the loops, saving some CPU.
    
    Moving forward, we can note that while some resources may not expose
    NUMA affinity (device plugins, extended resources), all resources must
    be reported at node level anyway; thus, if they are not present
    at node level, we can safely assume  we don't have the resource at all.
    
    Leveraging this allows us to further clean the core filtering logic.
    
