    Signed-off-by: Francesco Romani <fromani@redhat.com>
    
    * nrt: doc: document the NRT fundamental prerequisite
    
    A fundamental assumption for NRT to work correctly is that
    all the worker nodes must have a consistent NUMA topology
    and kubelet configuration.
    
    While the former prerequisite is not so strict and can be relaxed,
    a heteregenous host HW can lead to surprising (but not wrong) scheduling
    decisions, so we don't recommend it at this point in time.
    
    On the other hand, a consistent kubelet configuration it's a
    prerequisite, because it can lead to a bad scheduling decision.
    
    Unfortunately, it's very hard to detect inconsistencies at scheduling
    run time, and it's also unfeasible to enforce these prerequisite -
    the scheduler (or the NodeResourceTopology CRD!) is just the wrong
    place to do that.
    
    So, the only option left is to explicitely document this
    prerequisite and point cluster administrators to existing kubernetes
    tools which will enable them to deal with mixed HW topology and/or
    mixed kubelet configuration.
    
    Signed-off-by: Francesco Romani <fromani@redhat.com>

