    Score plugin for topology aware scheduler
    
        Score plugin allows the topology-aware scheduler to have better pod scheduling decisions.
        By ranking all suitable nodes based on a certain scoring strategy, the scheduler will be able to select the finest node as the candidate for the pod assignment.
    
        Available strategies are:
    
        "Most Allocated": Favors node with the least amount of available resource.
        "Balanced Allocation": Favors nodes with balanced resource usage rate.
        "Least Allocated": Favors node with the most amount of available resource
        All strategies are a simplified version of the in-tree Kubernetes noderesources scheduling plugins
        https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/tree/master/pkg/scheduler/framework/plugins/noderesources
    
        Proposal doc:
        https://drive.google.com/file/d/1XqCqRvvTLdt7uFzfCkLxPW139ojJm3AM/view?usp=sharing
    
        KEP:
        https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/scheduler-plugins/tree/master/kep/119-node-resource-topology-aware-scheduling
    
        Co-authored-by: Wei Huang <weih@hey.com>
        Signed-off-by: Talor Itzhak <titzhak@redhat.com>

